---
import WorksheetLayout from '../../../../layouts/WorksheetLayout.astro';
---
<WorksheetLayout
  title="Paper Circuit Practice"
  lesson="/courses/mfedu-2026/paper-circuits/"
  intro="Lay copper tape along the thick gray paths, leave gaps for your LEDs, and light all three circuits."
>
  <h2>1. Simple circuit — one path, one LED</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 700 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Simple circuit template: a rectangular tape path with one battery position and one LED gap" style="width:100%; height:auto;">
    <path d="M80 60 H620 V200 H80 Z" stroke="#D7D7D7" stroke-width="16" fill="none"/>
    <circle cx="80" cy="130" r="34" fill="none" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    <text x="52" y="136" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="15" fill="#474747">battery</text>
    <rect x="600" y="105" width="46" height="50" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    <text x="588" y="90" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="15" fill="#474747">LED gap</text>
  </svg>

  <h2>2. Parallel circuit — every LED gets its own path</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 700 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Parallel circuit template: two rails with three rungs, each rung has an LED gap" style="width:100%; height:auto;">
    <path d="M80 60 H620 M80 240 H620" stroke="#D7D7D7" stroke-width="16" fill="none"/>
    <path d="M80 60 V240 M300 60 V125 M300 175 V240 M470 60 V125 M470 175 V240 M620 60 V125 M620 175 V240" stroke="#D7D7D7" stroke-width="16" fill="none"/>
    <circle cx="80" cy="150" r="34" fill="none" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    <text x="52" y="156" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="15" fill="#474747">battery</text>
    {[300, 470, 620].map(x => (
      <rect x={x - 23} y="125" width="46" height="50" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    ))}
  </svg>

  <h2>3. Series circuit — one path through every LED</h2>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 700 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Series circuit template: one loop with two LED gaps along the top" style="width:100%; height:auto;">
    <path d="M80 60 H250 M330 60 H470 M550 60 H620 V200 H80 Z" stroke="#D7D7D7" stroke-width="16" fill="none"/>
    <circle cx="80" cy="130" r="34" fill="none" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    <text x="52" y="136" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="15" fill="#474747">battery</text>
    <rect x="252" y="35" width="76" height="50" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
    <rect x="472" y="35" width="76" height="50" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#474747" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
  </svg>

  <h2>Observations</h2>
  <p>Which circuit lit brightest? What happened when you removed one LED from the parallel circuit — and from the series circuit?</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>

  <ul class="ws-checks">
    <li>Positive tape path never touches the negative path (no short circuits!)</li>
    <li>Long LED legs on the positive side, short legs on the negative</li>
    <li>All three circuits lit</li>
  </ul>
</WorksheetLayout>
